// pfodWeb NOTE (button/LED/NeoPixel tagging + dedicated-hardware pin
// exclusion audit, 2026-07-13):
//
// Board: DatanoiseTV "PicoADK v2" (Pico Audio Dev Kit, second-generation
// hardware) - an RP2350A-based audio-DSP/synthesizer development board,
// successor to the RP2040-based "datanoisetv_picoadk" (v1) already
// audited this session (see variants/rp2040/rp2040/datanoisetv_picoadk/
// board.json and boardsDetails/rp2040/rp2040/datanoisetv_picoadk/notes.txt).
// v2 adds onboard 8MB QSPI PSRAM and a microSD card slot (SDIO 4-bit
// mode) not present on v1, and simplifies the LED story down to a single
// "user LED" (no confirmed 4-LED debug bank or WS2812 "Big Debug LED"
// like v1 - see GPIO2 finding below).
//
// Sources consulted (WebSearch/WebFetch, 2026-07-13):
//  1. https://www.cnx-software.com/2024/10/28/picoadk-v2-music-synthesizer-raspberry-pi-rp2350-board-audio-experimentation/
//     - CNX Software launch article. Quoted: "4 MB QSPI Flash for your
//     Code and Data"; "Optional 8MB QSPI PSRAM for applications which
//     needs more RAM (e.g. Long Delays)"; "TF-Card (Micro) on the bottom
//     of the PCB (SPI or SDIO 4-bit Mode capable)"; "I2S Pins exposed on
//     the headers, to allow for connecting an ADC"; "MIDI In Circuit with
//     Optocoupler"; "Power and user LEDs"; "SWD Debug Port".
//  2. https://circuitpython.org/board/datanoise_picoadk_v2/ - official
//     CircuitPython board listing for this exact board id. Confirms
//     "Power and user LEDs" (i.e. two LEDs total: a power-indicator LED
//     and a single software-controllable user LED) - no WS2812/NeoPixel/
//     addressable-RGB LED mentioned anywhere for v2, unlike v1's
//     ambiguous "Big Debug LED (WS2812 on v1.1a)".
//  3. https://github.com/DatanoiseTV/PicoADK-Firmware-Template - firmware
//     template README (fetched via WebFetch) explicitly contrasts v1 vs
//     v2 hardware: PSRAM "None (v1)" vs "8 MB QSPI (v2)"; SD Card "SPI
//     (v1)" vs "SDIO 4-bit (v2)"; MIDI "USB + DIN (v1)" vs "USB + DIN +
//     USB host (PIO USB) (v2)". Corroborates this board's own
//     pins_arduino.h PSRAM/SDIO/MIDI definitions independently of the
//     CNX Software article.
//  4. This board's own variants/rp2040/rp2350/datanoisetv_picoadk_v2/
//     pins_arduino.h - already carries a pre-existing "pfodWeb NOTE"
//     comment (present before this audit) stating D0/D15-D18/D20-D22 are
//     "deliberately NOT declared... all dedicated to onboard hardware,
//     not general-purpose" (PSRAM CS / I2S bus to the onboard DAC / SDIO
//     SD-card lines respectively), and that D1 (MIDI_RX) "is kept - it's
//     a normal external MIDI-in connector, not an internal bus." This
//     audit independently verified each of these claims against sources
//     #1-#3 above rather than taking the pre-existing comment at face
//     value, and found no discrepancy - only extended it with explicit
//     chipGpios documentation entries (GPIO23-25 SDIO D1-D3 were not yet
//     covered by an explicit entry) and the GPIO2 LED tagging (not yet
//     assessed at all).
//  5. rp2040/rp2040/datanoisetv_picoadk (v1 sibling) board.json + notes.txt
//     - structural precedent (capabilities:[] entries added purely for
//     documentation on already-excluded/alias-less GPIOs) and the direct
//     source of the "same vendor, same GPIO2 number" inference used below
//     for polarity (v1's PIN_LED0/GPIO2 was independently confirmed
//     active-high via github.com/DatanoiseTV/PicoADK-Hardware's
//     GettingStarted_Arduino.md: `digitalWrite(PIN_LED0, 1)` turns it on).
//  6. rp2040/rp2040/rpipico/board.json and rp2040/rp2350/rpipico2/board.json
//     - established precedent of checking the official Raspberry Pi
//     pico-sdk board header (boards/include/boards/pico.h, pico2.h) for
//     PICO_DEFAULT_LED_PIN / PICO_DEFAULT_LED_PIN_INVERTED as a direct
//     polarity source. Checked for this board: neither
//     raspberrypi/pico-sdk nor earlephilhower/arduino-pico's bundled
//     pico-sdk copy contains a "datanoisetv_picoadk_v2.h" (or similarly
//     named) board header (both raw-file fetches 404'd) - this
//     third-party board has no pico-sdk-level board definition, only the
//     arduino-pico pins_arduino.h/boards.txt entry. No direct-datasheet
//     polarity confirmation available for GPIO2 on v2 specifically (see
//     GPIO2 finding below for how this gap was handled).
//  7. pfodWeb_src/build_boards.js (parseEsp32Consts()/buildEsp32Board(),
//     read directly, not required/executed) - re-confirmed for this board
//     that (a) the pin sweep is driven purely by `static const uint8_t`
//     alias declarations found anywhere in the .h file, unioned with
//     chipGpios keys - NOT bounded by PINS_COUNT/NUM_DIGITAL_PINS (that
//     bound only applies to the separate AVR-style parser) - so GPIO23-25
//     (SDIO D1-D3) needed their own explicit chipGpios entries below to
//     stay properly documented/excluded, contrary to this board's own
//     pins_arduino.h comment's claim that they're "already excluded by
//     the conservative default pin range" (that claim does not hold for
//     this rp2040-family parser path); and (b) the
//     i2c_sda/i2c_scl/spi_ss/spi_mosi/spi_miso/spi_sck auto-append only
//     fires off the UNQUALIFIED `consts.SDA`/`SCL`/`SS`/`MOSI`/`MISO`/
//     `SCK` static-const aliases. GPIO2 (this board's only confirmed LED)
//     carries no such alias (SPI0_SS=GPIO5, SPI0_SCK=GPIO6,
//     SPI0_MOSI=GPIO7, SPI0_MISO=GPIO8/WIRE0_SDA, WIRE0_SCL=GPIO9,
//     WIRE1_SDA=GPIO6, WIRE1_SCL=GPIO7, SPI1_SCK/MOSI/MISO/SS=GPIO10-13) -
//     so the "confirmed button/LED pin also aliased as
//     SDA/SCL/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK" bug class flagged in this audit's task
//     brief was checked and does NOT fire on this board - no pins_arduino.h
//     edit was made or needed.
//
// GPIO0 (RP2350_PSRAM_CS / PIN_PSRAM_CS): CHANGED (excluded).
// capabilities: []. Dedicated chip-select line to the onboard 8MB QSPI
// PSRAM chip, confirmed via sources #1/#3 (v2-exclusive feature vs v1).
// No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h (already
// invisible/excluded by default per its own pre-existing comment) -
// entry added purely for documentation, matching v1's established
// pattern (source #5).
//
// GPIO1 (PIN_MIDI_RX): NO CHANGE. Kept - D1 alias already declared. A
// normal external MIDI-In DIN-connector signal routed through an
// optocoupler ("MIDI In Circuit with Optocoupler" per source #1), not an
// onboard-hardware control line - matches this board's own pre-existing
// pins_arduino.h comment and the analogous treatment of v1's
// header-exposed external signals (source #5).
//
// GPIO2 (PIN_LED / LED_BUILTIN): CHANGED. Tagged
// ["digital_output","pwm_output","led_high"]. Confirmed as a genuine
// onboard software-controllable "user LED" (as distinct from a separate,
// presumably-hardwired "power LED" with no GPIO) via source #1's "Power
// and user LEDs" and source #2's identical wording on the official
// CircuitPython board page for this exact board id. Critically, no
// source found for v2 mentions WS2812/NeoPixel/addressable RGB for this
// LED (unlike v1's explicitly-flagged-ambiguous GPIO15 "Big Debug LED
// (WS2812 on v1.1a)") - only a single plain "user LED" is documented for
// v2, and this board's pins_arduino.h itself only ever aliases GPIO2 as
// PIN_LED/LED_BUILTIN (no PIO/NeoPixel-library scaffolding referenced
// anywhere), so led_neopixel is not a candidate here. Active-high
// polarity could NOT be independently confirmed from a v2-specific
// datasheet or vendor code sample (source #6 - no pico-sdk board header
// exists for this third-party board to check
// PICO_DEFAULT_LED_PIN_INVERTED against, and no v2-specific blink/LED
// example was found in the vendor's firmware-template repo). Tagged
// led_high anyway based on two converging, explicitly-flagged inferences
// rather than a blind guess: (a) this is the exact same vendor
// (DatanoiseTV) and the exact same GPIO number (GPIO2) used for v1's
// PIN_LED0, which WAS independently confirmed active-high via the
// vendor's own GettingStarted_Arduino.md (source #5) - a direct-successor
// product reusing the pin number strongly suggests the same simple
// GPIO-resistor-LED-GND direct-drive circuit; (b) every single RP2040/
// RP2350 board's LED_BUILTIN pin audited in this session's family sweep
// so far (rpipico, adafruit_macropad2040, akana_r1, rpipico2, v1
// datanoisetv_picoadk) has been independently confirmed led_high with
// zero led_low exceptions found for a plain (non-multiplexed,
// non-WiFi-chip-routed) onboard LED - a 100% consistent chip-family
// convention. digital_input dropped to match this repo's established
// led_high precedent; pwm_output kept since analogWrite() works on any
// RP2040/RP2350 GPIO. No SDA/SCL/SPI alias collision on GPIO2 (see
// source #7) - nothing to fix in pins_arduino.h.
//
// GPIO15 (PIN_I2S_DIN): CHANGED (excluded). capabilities: []. I2S
// data-IN line - new vs v1 (which had no DIN, being a playback-only I2S
// DAC target). Consistent with source #1's "I2S Pins exposed on the
// headers, to allow for connecting an ADC" and this board's own
// pre-existing pins_arduino.h comment grouping D15-D18 together as "the
// I2S bus to the onboard DAC". No static-const alias in pins_arduino.h -
// already excluded by default; entry added purely for documentation.
//
// GPIO16 (PIN_I2S_DOUT), GPIO17 (PIN_I2S_BCLK), GPIO18 (PIN_I2S_LRCLK):
// CHANGED (excluded). capabilities: [] each. Dedicated I2S data-out/
// bit-clock/word-select lines to the onboard audio codec/DAC, per
// sources #1/#3/#4 (same treatment as GPIO15 above - part of the same
// 4-wire I2S bus). No static-const aliases in pins_arduino.h - already
// excluded by default; entries added purely for documentation.
//
// GPIO20 (PIN_SDIO_CLK), GPIO21 (PIN_SDIO_CMD), GPIO22 (PIN_SDIO_D0),
// GPIO23 (PIN_SDIO_D1), GPIO24 (PIN_SDIO_D2), GPIO25 (PIN_SDIO_D3):
// CHANGED (excluded). capabilities: [] each. Dedicated microSD card SDIO
// 4-bit-mode bus (CLK/CMD/D0-D3), confirmed v2-exclusive feature per
// sources #1 ("TF-Card (Micro)... SDIO 4-bit Mode capable") and #3
// ("SD Card:... SDIO 4-bit (v2)" vs "SPI (v1)"). No static-const aliases
// anywhere in pins_arduino.h for any of these six GPIOs - already
// excluded by default (this board's own pre-existing comment already
// flagged D20-D22; GPIO23-25 lacked an explicit chipGpios entry before
// this audit, added now per source #7's finding that the parser isn't
// actually bounded by PINS_COUNT the way the pre-existing pins_arduino.h
// comment assumed - added purely for documentation/completeness, no
// functional change since they were already unreachable without an
// alias).
//
// GPIO3, GPIO4 (D3, D4): NO CHANGE. Ordinary spare GPIOs. No source
// consulted documents any onboard hardware on these two pins for v2 (v1's
// GPIO3/4 were part of its 4-LED debug bank per source #5, but no
// equivalent multi-LED bank is documented anywhere for v2 - see GPIO2
// finding above). Left at full chip-default capability.
//
// GPIO5 (PIN_SPI0_SS), GPIO6 (PIN_SPI0_SCK / PIN_WIRE1_SDA), GPIO7
// (PIN_SPI0_MOSI / PIN_WIRE1_SCL), GPIO8 (PIN_SPI0_MISO / PIN_WIRE0_SDA),
// GPIO9 (PIN_WIRE0_SCL), GPIO10 (PIN_SPI1_SCK), GPIO11 (PIN_SPI1_MOSI):
// NO CHANGE. Ordinary dual-role SPI0/SPI1/Wire0/Wire1 header-exposed
// pins (D5-D11 all declared) - no internal-signal source consulted
// mentions any of these as connected to fixed onboard hardware (unlike
// v1's GPIO10-13, which the v1 vendor README explicitly documented as
// also driving an onboard SPI ADC chip). Left at full chip-default
// capability; the automatic i2c_sda/i2c_scl/spi_sck/spi_mosi/spi_miso/
// spi_ss capability auto-append on GPIO6-9 (via build_boards.js's
// unqualified SDA/SCL resolution) and GPIO5/10/11 is expected/correct
// behaviour for general-purpose bus pins, not the alias-collision bug
// class (see source #7 - none of these GPIOs is tagged button/LED).
//
// GPIO12 (PIN_SPI1_MISO / PIN_SERIAL1_TX), GPIO13 (PIN_SPI1_SS /
// PIN_SERIAL1_RX): NO CHANGE. build_boards.js's TX/RX early-return path
// (checked directly in source #7) forces these to serial_tx/serial_rx
// capability only, taking priority over any SPI1 bus auto-append -
// pre-existing default behaviour, not specific to this audit.
//
// GPIO14, GPIO19 (D14, D19): NO CHANGE. Ordinary spare GPIOs, no alias
// beyond the plain D-number, not mentioned in any source consulted as
// connected to onboard hardware (GPIO19 was part of v1's reused-SPI0/I2S
// exclusion, but v2's I2S bus lives entirely on GPIO15-18 instead - see
// pins_arduino.h; GPIO19 here is a genuine spare pin, not grouped with
// any bus). Left at full chip-default capability.
//
// GPIO26 (A0), GPIO27 (A1 / PIN_SERIAL2_TX), GPIO28 (A2 /
// PIN_SERIAL2_RX): NO CHANGE. Ordinary analog/dual-role UART2 header
// pins, not mentioned in any source consulted as connected to onboard
// hardware. Left at full chip-default capability.
//
// "Power LED" (per sources #1/#2): out of scope, not a missed tag. No
// GPIO alias or internal-signal source suggests this is software-
// controlled - power-indicator LEDs on dev boards are conventionally
// hardwired directly across the supply rail through a series resistor,
// not GPIO-driven, and no source consulted contradicts that default
// assumption for this board. No pin exists in pins_arduino.h to attach a
// capability to (same "out of scope" treatment as the BOOTSEL button on
// rpipico/rpipico2 - source #6).
//
// Full findings/sources trail:
// boardsDetails/rp2040/rp2350/datanoisetv_picoadk_v2/notes.txt
{
  // Output filename and BoardLoader data-variable name:
  //   boardName "RP2350" -> designer/boards/RP2350/RP2350.json -> const RP2350Data = {...}
  "boardName": "RP2350",

  // Fallback human-readable name shown in the designer UI.  Overridden
  // by the matching `<id>.name=` entry in a sibling-or-ancestor
  // boards.txt when one is present (matched via `<id>.build.variant=`
  // against this variant's directory name).
  "displayName": "Raspberry Pi Pico 2 (RP2350)",

  // Same parser dialect as every other RP2040/RP2350 board — see
  // ../board.json for the full rationale.
  "family": "rp2040",

  // This board's own pins_arduino.h declares no capacitive/mechanical
  // button aliases, and RP2350 boots from an internal ROM/BOOTSEL, not a
  // GPIO-driven flash-mode strapping pin — no boot-time restrictions or
  // button pin to flag at the chip level.
  "inputOnlyGpios": [],

  // Default transports — Serial only (plain RP2350A audio board, no
  // onboard WiFi chip).
  "connections": ["serial"],

  "pinNotes": {},

  "chipGpios": {
    "0":  { "capabilities": [], "note": "RP2350_PSRAM_CS / PIN_PSRAM_CS - dedicated chip-select line to the onboard 8MB QSPI PSRAM chip (v2-exclusive feature vs v1, per DatanoiseTV/PicoADK-Firmware-Template README). No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "2":  { "capabilities": ["digital_output", "pwm_output", "led_high"], "note": "PIN_LED / LED_BUILTIN - onboard \"user LED\" per circuitpython.org/board/datanoise_picoadk_v2/ and the CNX Software v2 launch article (\"Power and user LEDs\" - no WS2812/NeoPixel mentioned for v2). Active-high polarity inferred (not independently confirmed for v2 - no pico-sdk board header exists for this third-party board): same vendor + same GPIO number as v1's PIN_LED0 (independently confirmed active-high), and 100% led_high precedent across every other RP2040/RP2350 LED_BUILTIN audited this session (rpipico, adafruit_macropad2040, akana_r1, rpipico2, v1 datanoisetv_picoadk)." },
    "15": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_I2S_DIN - I2S data-IN line to/from the onboard audio codec bus (new vs v1, which had no DIN). No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "16": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_I2S_DOUT - I2S data-out line, part of the onboard audio codec bus. No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "17": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_I2S_BCLK - I2S bit-clock line, part of the onboard audio codec bus. No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "18": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_I2S_LRCLK - I2S word-select (LR clock) line, part of the onboard audio codec bus. No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "20": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SDIO_CLK - onboard microSD card SDIO bus clock line (v2-exclusive feature vs v1's SPI-only SD wiring). No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "21": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SDIO_CMD - onboard microSD card SDIO bus command line. No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "22": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SDIO_D0 - onboard microSD card SDIO bus data line 0. No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "23": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SDIO_D1 - onboard microSD card SDIO bus data line 1 (4-bit mode). No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "24": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SDIO_D2 - onboard microSD card SDIO bus data line 2 (4-bit mode). No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "25": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SDIO_D3 - onboard microSD card SDIO bus data line 3 (4-bit mode). No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." }
  },

  // Same 8-bit analogWrite() default as every other RP2040/RP2350 board.
  "pwm": { "min": 0, "max": 255, "method": "analogWrite" },

  // No hardware DAC on RP2350 silicon itself (this board's 32-bit audio
  // output goes through the onboard I2S audio codec/DAC chip via
  // GPIO15-18, not the RP2350's own silicon).
  "dac": {},

  // 3 analog channels (A0-A2 = GPIO26-28), 12-bit ADC - matches the
  // chip-level default and this board's own pins_arduino.h
  // (NUM_ANALOG_INPUTS=3, ADC_RESOLUTION=12).
  "adc": { "bits": 12, "max": 4095, "defaultRefVolts": "3.3" }
}
